    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25xjkSizeFBrzHTULVxNtCU)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- **Stacked on #513** (base branch `513-cite-open-devonthink-record`): it uses `sp-cite-open` (the PDF's reference list) which only exists there. Merge #513 first; GitHub then retargets this PR to `main`.\n- #513 currently has conflicts with `main`; resolve them there, then this PR needs at most a merge of `main`.\n- If merged before #513: not possible, the base is that branch.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New module `sp-sourcerefs` (literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-sourcerefs.org`, bullets) and `tests/sp-sourcerefs-test.el`.\n- A line `SOURCEREFS text` (optionally after a list bullet) in a litnote is a reference met in the PDF you are reading.\n- `M-x sp-sourcerefs-convert` (`C-c o s`), on the region or the buffer:\n  - looks for the PDF's reference list: the litnote's citekey (`#+reference:` or `ROAM_REFS`) must equal the citekey of the record in front in DEVONthink; a short `Smith 2017` is widened to the full entry (`sp-cite-open-entry`);\n  - matches every line with `sp-cite-match` (BibTeX files, same thresholds); no second matcher;\n  - shows a report buffer and asks once;\n  - clear matches become `[cite:@key]` (bullet kept), close calls ask you to choose, unmatched lines stay as they are;\n  - matched works and unmatched lines go to the `Cited works` table (`sp-cite-match-write-section`): the `TODO unmatched` rows and works without a litnote are what to read next.\n- Design doc, README module table and the `require` in `sp-academic` updated. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Checked by Claude\n\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: 5 ERT tests pass (collecting lines, region, bullet kept on replace, citekey, end-to-end with the matcher and the table writer stubbed); `check-parens` OK.\n- Not run: the real matcher on your `.bib` files with this command, the DEVONthink reference list (macOS), litdb fallback (not used here), the Cited works table in a real litnote.\n\n## Not covered / open questions\n\n- Capture of a `SOURCEREFS` line from a selection in DEVONthink (`Caps+r` opens a record; it does not write the line).\n- litdb is not used as a fallback for unmatched lines (it is a list to pick from, so left out).\n- A converted line loses its original text (undo restores it). Should the original be kept, e.g. as `[cite:@key] (was: ...)`?\n- The cross-litnote \"read next\" ranking from the design doc is not built; the table is per litnote.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `emacs -Q --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-sourcerefs-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes\n- [ ] In a litnote, add `- SOURCEREFS Smith 2017` (a work you have in BibTeX) and `- SOURCEREFS Nobody 1900 Unknown`; `C-c o s`: a report shows `accept` and `none`; answer `y`\n- [ ] The first line becomes `- [cite:@key]`; the second stays; a `Cited works` table appears with the work and a `TODO unmatched` row\n- [ ] Run it again: nothing duplicates in the table; \"No SOURCEREFS lines\" for the converted ones\n- [ ] With the PDF open in DEVONthink (same citekey as `#+reference:`), a short `SOURCEREFS (Smith 2017)` is matched through the PDF's reference list\n- [ ] Select two lines, `C-c o s`: only those are converted\n- [ ] `C-/` after converting restores the lines\n- [ ] `C-c o X` with the filter `SOURCEREFS` still lists the unconverted lines\n- [ ] Regression: `Ctrl+Shift+K` and `Caps+r` in DEVONthink behave as in #513\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9taQEBJAWpQmkyfLY)_",
